WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
Is dirt just dirt?

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.520
This cloudy jar holds soil and water.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.340
After a shake and a day or two of settling, the soil forms layers.

4
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.773
It takes about twenty minutes, plus a few quick looks later.

5
00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:21.153
Your child practices looking closely, making a guess, and checking it.

6
00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:24.773
They also practice waiting for a slow result.

7
00:00:26.053 --> 00:00:27.773
And they find out that soil is a mix.

8
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:32.473
You need a clear plastic jar with a lid that screws on tight.

9
00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:39.133
Never use glass. Bring about one to one and a half cups of bagged topsoil.

10
00:00:40.213 --> 00:00:42.953
Add water, masking tape, a marker, and a ruler.

11
00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:47.227
Stay with your child while the soil and water are out.

12
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.507
Spread a spoonful of soil on white paper.

13
00:00:51.747 --> 00:00:53.907
Look for rock, roots, and leaves together.

14
00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:57.527
Ask, 'Does it feel gritty, smooth, or sticky?'

15
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.760
Before any water goes in, ask, 'If we shake soil in water and wait, what will it

16
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.040
look like?' Have your child draw a guess.

17
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.380
Keep it to check later.

18
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:12.133
Pick out sticks and stones bigger than a pea.

19
00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.253
Fill the jar about one third full of soil.

20
00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:19.153
Slowly add water to about one inch from the top.

21
00:01:20.453 --> 00:01:21.453
Watch for bubbles.

22
00:01:22.513 --> 00:01:24.993
That is air that was in the spaces in the soil.

23
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:27.487
Tighten and check the lid.

24
00:01:28.807 --> 00:01:32.187
Take turns shaking hard over a towel for two to three minutes.

25
00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:37.087
Have your child sit or stand over the towel and grip with both hands.

26
00:01:38.327 --> 00:01:41.007
For ages five to seven, you do the long shaking.

27
00:01:42.087 --> 00:01:44.327
Set the jar on a low, steady surface.

28
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.410
Here is a question for you.

29
00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.530
Inside that cloudy jar are big grains of sand, finer silt, and tiny bits of clay.

30
00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.350
Which do you think settles first?

31
00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.590
Which takes the longest?

32
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.850
The big bits sink first.

33
00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.930
After about one minute, sand forms the bottom layer.

34
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.430
Your child marks its top with a strip of tape.

35
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:19.430
Dark bits floating on the water are usually old plant parts on their way to becoming

36
00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.430
humus.

37
00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.970
After one hour, look for silt above the sand and mark it with tape.

38
00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.090
After one to two days, look for clay above it.

39
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.470
Measure any layers you can see in centimeters.

40
00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.850
Clay-rich soil can stay cloudy for days.

41
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.930
Set the first drawing beside the jar.

42
00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.670
Ask, 'What matched your guess?'

43
00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.150
Use the layers to talk about which bits sank first and what is still floating.

44
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.070
Small stones can choke children under four, so keep them from babies and toddlers.

45
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.650
If a child is choking, call nine one one.

46
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.770
Nobody puts soil or muddy fingers in a mouth.

47
00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.490
Wash hands with soap afterward.

48
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.763
Bagged topsoil is the safest choice.

49
00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:11.763
If you plan to dig in a garden, read the guide's soil safety notes before choosing a

50
00:03:11.763 --> 00:03:12.763
spot.

51
00:03:13.117 --> 00:03:15.457
That brown stuff on your shoes is a mix.

52
00:03:16.757 --> 00:03:20.937
Your child saw the bigger grains settle first and the smaller bits take longer.
